0
00:00:07,812 --> 00:00:10,582
PREVIOUSLY ON
"AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL"--

1
00:00:10,582 --> 00:00:12,350
WHEN BRE'S GRANOLA BARS
WENT MISSING...

2
00:00:12,350 --> 00:00:13,351
THAT WAS NICE.
WHO DID THAT?

3
00:00:20,225 --> 00:00:22,327
SHE WENT ON
THE WARPATH AGAINST NICOLE.

4
00:00:22,327 --> 00:00:24,463
I POURED OUT ALL
OF NICOLE'S CANNED SODAS.

5
00:00:24,463 --> 00:00:26,898
I'VE BEEN DISRESPECTED,
BUT THIS WAS JUST TOO MUCH.

6
00:00:26,898 --> 00:00:29,267
BUT BOTH GIRLS MANAGED
TO SET ASIDE THE DRAMA

7
00:00:29,267 --> 00:00:31,269
AND TURN IN
FIERCE PHOTOS...

8
00:00:31,269 --> 00:00:32,604
THAT'S IT-- YOU'RE LOVELY
LIKE THAT.

9
00:00:32,604 --> 00:00:33,972
KEEP THAT POISE. LOVELY.

10
00:00:33,972 --> 00:00:35,941
WHILE KIM FAILED
TO DELIVER.

11
00:00:35,941 --> 00:00:39,311
I DON'T THINK THAT KIM HAS
GIVEN ME ANY AMAZING PICTURES.

12
00:00:39,311 --> 00:00:41,713
KIM, WE DON'T SEE
CONSISTENCY IN YOU.

13
00:00:41,713 --> 00:00:43,315
AND SHE WAS
SENT HOME.

14
00:00:43,315 --> 00:00:44,516
FOUR GIRLS REMAIN.

15
00:00:44,516 --> 00:00:46,418
WHO WILL BE ELIMINATED
TONIGHT?

16
00:00:46,418 --> 00:00:49,721
♪♪♪

17
00:01:33,331 --> 00:01:34,833
I JUST GOT BACK
FROM ELIMINATION.

18
00:01:34,833 --> 00:01:37,536
INSTEAD OF BRE BEING ELIMINATED
LIKE I THOUGHT WOULD HAPPEN,

19
00:01:37,536 --> 00:01:40,205
KIM GOT ELIMINATED.

20
00:01:40,205 --> 00:01:41,873
I DON'T REALLY
TRUST BRE FULLY

21
00:01:41,873 --> 00:01:44,276
BECAUSE OF ALL THE THINGS
SHE'S PULLED.

22
00:01:44,276 --> 00:01:45,510
I DON'T FEEL COMFORTABLE
WITH YOU, LIKE,

23
00:01:45,510 --> 00:01:46,845
STEALING
MY THINGS.

24
00:01:46,845 --> 00:01:47,946
WHERE IS
YOUR STUFF AT?

25
00:01:47,946 --> 00:01:49,481
YOU DRANK IT,
AND YOU STOLE IT.

26
00:01:49,481 --> 00:01:50,749
THAT'S STEALING, BRE.

27
00:01:50,749 --> 00:01:51,817
YOUR RED BULLS
ARE GONE.

28
00:01:51,817 --> 00:01:52,918
SO IS MY GRANOLA.

29
00:01:52,918 --> 00:01:54,586
WHAT DO YOU WANT ME
TO DO NOW?

30
00:01:54,586 --> 00:01:55,620
I WANT YOU
TO PAY FOR IT.

31
00:01:55,620 --> 00:01:56,721
I'M NOT.

32
00:01:56,721 --> 00:01:58,857
SO NOW
WHAT DO WE DO?

33
00:01:58,857 --> 00:02:00,926
I'M REALLY UPSET
THAT KIM LEFT.

34
00:02:00,926 --> 00:02:02,294
IT'S ALWAYS BETTER

35
00:02:02,294 --> 00:02:04,262
WHEN YOU HAVE, LIKE,
A GOOD FRIEND AROUND,

36
00:02:04,262 --> 00:02:06,264
AND THAT'S
WHAT SHE WAS.

37
00:02:06,264 --> 00:02:08,266
I'M GONNA MISS HER
IN THE HOUSE.

38
00:02:08,266 --> 00:02:09,301
(sniffles)

39
00:02:14,773 --> 00:02:16,874
I'M TIRED OF PEOPLE
TAKING MY STUFF.

40
00:02:16,874 --> 00:02:18,877
I'M TIRED OF PEOPLE
BEING INCONSIDERATE.

41
00:02:18,877 --> 00:02:21,680
BRE AND NICOLE ARE REALLY
PISSED OFF AT EACH OTHER,

42
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:24,216
ALL OVER
A FRIGGIN' GRANOLA BAR.

43
00:02:24,216 --> 00:02:27,219
NOBODY SEES ME
HERE

44
00:02:27,219 --> 00:02:28,787
AS A GOOD
PERSON.

45
00:02:28,787 --> 00:02:30,555
AND I AM.

46
00:02:30,555 --> 00:02:32,190
I KNOW
NICOLE HATES ME.

47
00:02:32,190 --> 00:02:33,625
SHE DISLIKED ME
BEFORE,

48
00:02:33,625 --> 00:02:34,893
BUT I KNOW
SHE HATES ME NOW.

49
00:02:34,893 --> 00:02:37,562
TO KNOW THAT MY POSITION
IN THIS COMPETITION

50
00:02:37,562 --> 00:02:39,865
HAS
PRETTY MUCH BEEN TARNISHED

51
00:02:39,865 --> 00:02:42,334
OVER A STUPID
GRANOLA BAR--

52
00:02:42,334 --> 00:02:44,736
I KNOW I'M WRONG
FOR NOT APOLOGIZING,

53
00:02:44,736 --> 00:02:47,572
BUT I GUESS
I JUST DON'T CARE.

54
00:02:55,247 --> 00:02:57,249
I WAS IN THE BOTTOM TWO
TWICE IN A ROW,

55
00:02:57,249 --> 00:02:59,251
AND I WAS LIKE,
"WHAT THE HELL?"

56
00:02:59,251 --> 00:03:02,554
I'M EXTREMELY CONFUSED
BY THE ENTIRE COMPETITION.

57
00:03:02,554 --> 00:03:04,356
THERE'S GIRLS HERE

58
00:03:04,356 --> 00:03:06,258
THAT I THINK THAT I HAVE DONE
CONSISTENTLY BETTER THAN,

59
00:03:06,258 --> 00:03:07,893
AND THEY'RE DOING
BETTER THAN ME NOW.

60
00:03:07,893 --> 00:03:09,961
ALL THAT MATTERS IS
I'M STILL HERE,

61
00:03:09,961 --> 00:03:11,329
AND I STILL HAVE
ANOTHER CHANCE.

62
00:03:12,464 --> 00:03:14,432
TYRA MAIL!

63
00:03:15,533 --> 00:03:16,635
"GEAR UP FOR SCHOOL.

64
00:03:16,635 --> 00:03:18,536
"FIND OUT
AT 7 A.M.

65
00:03:18,536 --> 00:03:19,905
"DRESS THE PART,
PREPPY!"

66
00:03:19,905 --> 00:03:21,806
"FROM EVERY TWIG,
A FASHION MOVEMENT GROWS.

67
00:03:21,806 --> 00:03:23,308
"DRESS THE PART,
MON."

68
00:03:23,308 --> 00:03:24,743
"DRESS THE PART,
PUNK."

69
00:03:24,743 --> 00:03:26,511
"EAST IS WEST
AT 7 A.M.

70
00:03:26,511 --> 00:03:27,946
"DRESS THE PART,
BOLLYWOOD."

71
00:03:27,946 --> 00:03:29,347
WHAT IS
BOLLYWOOD?

72
00:03:29,347 --> 00:03:31,349
I WAS JUST
ASSUMING HOLLYWOOD.

73
00:03:31,349 --> 00:03:32,584
I DON'T KNOW.

74
00:03:32,584 --> 00:03:36,388
♪♪♪

75
00:03:36,388 --> 00:03:37,389
I DON'T KNOW.

76
00:03:37,389 --> 00:03:38,723
I COULD WEAR
A SKIRT.

77
00:03:38,723 --> 00:03:40,859
I REALLY DON'T KNOW
WHAT BOLLYWOOD IS.

78
00:03:40,859 --> 00:03:42,661
I DON'T KNOW
HOW TO BE PREPPY.

79
00:03:42,661 --> 00:03:44,296
I DON'T LIKE
DRESSING PREPPY.

80
00:03:44,296 --> 00:03:46,564
I DIDN'T EVEN DRESS PREPPY
WHEN I WAS IN SCHOOL, SO...

81
00:03:46,564 --> 00:03:48,366
DO YOU NORMALLY
WEAR PUNK?

82
00:03:48,366 --> 00:03:49,367
YES,
SHE DOES.

83
00:03:49,367 --> 00:03:50,669
I'M
THE PUNK FAN.

84
00:03:50,669 --> 00:03:53,672
I'M GOING TO THROW CLOTHES ON
AND WHATEVER-- I'M GOOD.

85
00:03:53,672 --> 00:03:55,674
MAKE SURE TO WEAR
YOUR SUNGLASSES.

86
00:03:55,674 --> 00:03:56,875
OKAY.

87
00:03:56,875 --> 00:03:58,276
'CAUSE I KNOW THAT
THAT'S MOD.

88
00:03:58,276 --> 00:03:59,411
I THINK,
OVERALL,

89
00:03:59,411 --> 00:04:01,680
I'M NOT THE ONLY ONE
WHO'S NERVOUS RIGHT NOW.

90
00:04:09,621 --> 00:04:11,589
GIRLS,
WELCOME TO CARNABY STREET.

91
00:04:11,589 --> 00:04:13,758
I'M SIMON DOONAN
FROM BARNEY'S,

92
00:04:13,758 --> 00:04:14,826
AND I'M GONNA
BE TEACHING YOU

93
00:04:14,826 --> 00:04:17,762
ALL ABOUT THE HISTORY
OF LONDON FASHION.

94
00:04:17,762 --> 00:04:19,564
NOW ARE YOU ALL FAMILIAR
WITH CARNABY STREET?

95
00:04:19,564 --> 00:04:22,300
(crickets chirping)

96
00:04:22,300 --> 00:04:23,335
(groans)

97
00:04:23,335 --> 00:04:24,769
THIS IS
WHERE IT ALL STARTED.

98
00:04:24,769 --> 00:04:26,603
IN THE 1960s,

99
00:04:26,603 --> 00:04:29,374
FASHION EXPLODED
HERE IN LONDON,

100
00:04:29,374 --> 00:04:30,475
AND THIS WAS
THE EPICENTER.

101
00:04:30,475 --> 00:04:31,910
SO TODAY

102
00:04:31,910 --> 00:04:34,846
YOU'RE GONNA BE LEARNING
ALL ABOUT LONDON FASHION.

103
00:04:34,846 --> 00:04:37,582
YOU'RE GONNA BE TESTED
ON EVERYTHING THAT YOU LEARN,

104
00:04:37,582 --> 00:04:38,950
AND IF
YOU'RE LUCKY,

105
00:04:38,950 --> 00:04:40,852
YOU COULD END UP
AS A MODEL ON CARNABY STREET.

106
00:04:40,852 --> 00:04:42,721
IF YOU'RE NOT,
YOU COULD END UP

107
00:04:42,721 --> 00:04:44,255
DOWN WITH THE STRIPPERS
IN SOHO.

108
00:04:44,255 --> 00:04:45,724
(laughing)

109
00:04:45,724 --> 00:04:46,725
JUST KIDDING.

110
00:04:46,725 --> 00:04:48,660
ANYWAY,
SO FOLLOW ME.

111
00:04:48,660 --> 00:04:52,263
♪♪♪

112
00:04:52,263 --> 00:04:54,265
SO YOU'RE PROBABLY WONDERING
WHERE THE HELL ARE WE?

113
00:04:54,265 --> 00:04:57,936
THIS IS AN EXHIBIT
WHICH SHOWS YOU

114
00:04:57,936 --> 00:05:00,705
ALL OF THE DIFFERENT TRENDS
AND IDEAS

115
00:05:00,705 --> 00:05:02,374
WHICH ARE
DRIVING BRITISH FASHION.

116
00:05:02,374 --> 00:05:05,243
AND WE'RE GONNA START
WITH THE MOST FUN-- BOLLYWOOD.

117
00:05:05,243 --> 00:05:08,179
IN INDIA, THERE'S A PLACE
CALLED BOLLYWOOD

118
00:05:08,179 --> 00:05:09,914
WHERE THEY MAKE
ALL THE INDIAN MOVIES.

119
00:05:09,914 --> 00:05:13,318
BOLLYWOOD IS
ABOUT EXCESS

120
00:05:13,318 --> 00:05:15,286
AND COLOR
AND SEQUINS.

121
00:05:15,286 --> 00:05:17,455
ONE OF YOU WAS INSTRUCTED
BY TYRA

122
00:05:17,455 --> 00:05:19,657
TO DRESS
IN THE STYLE OF BOLLYWOOD.

123
00:05:19,657 --> 00:05:21,559
I'M HAVING A LITTLE BIT
OF A HARD TIME

124
00:05:21,559 --> 00:05:23,495
FIGURING OUT
WHICH ONE THAT WAS,

125
00:05:23,495 --> 00:05:25,363
SO HELP ME OUT
HERE.

126
00:05:25,363 --> 00:05:26,498
IT WAS ME.

127
00:05:26,498 --> 00:05:27,766
OKAY.

128
00:05:27,766 --> 00:05:30,602
WHAT COULD HAVE BEEN GOOD
IS MAYBE

129
00:05:30,602 --> 00:05:33,271
IF YOU'D CHUCK
THIS SARI AROUND YOU.

130
00:05:33,271 --> 00:05:35,273
HOW DO YOU WANT ME
TO PUT THIS AROUND ME?

131
00:05:35,273 --> 00:05:37,208
I'M NOT
REALLY SURE.

132
00:05:37,208 --> 00:05:39,210
I DON'T REALLY KNOW
WHAT TO DO WITH THIS.

133
00:05:39,210 --> 00:05:40,945
UM...

134
00:05:40,945 --> 00:05:43,214
(laughs)

135
00:05:43,214 --> 00:05:45,183
I NEVER DO
THE RIGHT THING.

136
00:05:45,183 --> 00:05:47,185
WHY DON'T YOU
JUST CHUCK THIS AROUND.

137
00:05:47,185 --> 00:05:48,186
GREAT.

138
00:05:48,186 --> 00:05:49,320
YOU'RE TOTALLY
BOLLYWOOD.

139
00:05:49,320 --> 00:05:50,522
HERE WE ARE

140
00:05:50,522 --> 00:05:52,524
AT A COMPLETELY
DIFFERENT CONCEPT.

141
00:05:52,524 --> 00:05:53,925
HERE'S
THE PREPPY GIRL.

142
00:05:53,925 --> 00:05:55,493
SHE'S SNOTTY.
SHE'S RICH.

143
00:05:55,493 --> 00:05:58,630
SHE'S LOOKING DOWN
HER NOSE AT EVERYBODY.

144
00:05:58,630 --> 00:06:00,398
IT IS A VERY
CONSERVATIVE LOOK.

145
00:06:00,398 --> 00:06:01,566
IT'S ABOUT
TWIN SETS.

146
00:06:01,566 --> 00:06:02,667
IT'S ABOUT
SWEATER SETS.

147
00:06:02,667 --> 00:06:04,736
IT'S ABOUT
PLEATED SKIRTS.

148
00:06:04,736 --> 00:06:08,540
NOW ONE OF YOU WAS TOLD BY TYRA
TO DRESS PREPPY.

149
00:06:08,540 --> 00:06:10,308
NOW, NO OFFENSE,
BRE,

150
00:06:10,308 --> 00:06:11,910
BUT A CROTCH-LENGTH
DENIM SKIRT

151
00:06:11,910 --> 00:06:15,680
IS NOT THE LAST WORD
IN PREPPY ATTIRE.

152
00:06:15,680 --> 00:06:18,216
IT'S SORT OF
PREPPIE GOES SLUTTY.

153
00:06:18,216 --> 00:06:19,417
(chuckles)

154
00:06:19,417 --> 00:06:20,785
SO MANY MODELS
TODAY

155
00:06:20,785 --> 00:06:22,954
WALK AROUND DRESSED
LIKE HOOCHIE DANCERS.

156
00:06:22,954 --> 00:06:25,623
AND THEY NEED TO BE
A LITTLE MORE CONSERVATIVE

157
00:06:25,623 --> 00:06:27,192
THAN THEY
USUALLY ARE.

158
00:06:27,192 --> 00:06:28,927
(punk rock playing)

159
00:06:28,927 --> 00:06:35,333
GIRLS, WELCOME TO THE ANGRY,
CRAZY, MANIACAL WORLD OF PUNK.

160
00:06:35,333 --> 00:06:38,903
THE THING ABOUT PUNK WAS
IT WAS A VERY VIOLENT THING.

161
00:06:38,903 --> 00:06:40,905
THERE WERE GIRLS
WEARING TRASH BAGS

162
00:06:40,905 --> 00:06:42,907
WITH SAFETY PINS
THROUGH THEIR CHEEKS.

163
00:06:42,907 --> 00:06:47,278
ONE OF YOU WAS ASKED BY TYRA
TO DRESS PUNK.

164
00:06:47,278 --> 00:06:50,181
OH, IT'S THE JAPANESE SCHOOLGIRL
ON THE END.

165
00:06:50,181 --> 00:06:52,717
WELL, THIS IS
A VERY SORT OF PRISSY PUNK.

166
00:06:52,717 --> 00:06:54,352
NO OFFENSE.

167
00:06:54,352 --> 00:06:58,389
AS A PUNK,
JAYLA WAS A COMPLETE DISASTER.

168
00:06:59,858 --> 00:07:01,192
OKAY,
GIRLS.

169
00:07:01,192 --> 00:07:04,696
IT'S TIME TO GO
STARK RAVING MOD.

170
00:07:04,696 --> 00:07:06,865
NOW I KNOW A LOT
ABOUT MOD.

171
00:07:06,865 --> 00:07:11,503
BUT THERE'S SOMEBODY WHO KNOWS
A HELL OF A LOT MORE THAN ME--

172
00:07:11,503 --> 00:07:12,937
THE CREATOR
OF IT ALL,

173
00:07:12,937 --> 00:07:15,907
THE EPICENTER
OF MOD-- TWIGGY.

174
00:07:15,907 --> 00:07:16,908
AND
I'M HERE.

175
00:07:16,908 --> 00:07:17,909
HELLO, GIRLS.

176
00:07:17,909 --> 00:07:19,644
HELLO,
LOVE.

177
00:07:19,644 --> 00:07:21,546
I KNOW I AM NOT MOD
AT ALL.

178
00:07:21,546 --> 00:07:23,781
AND OUT POPS
TWIGGY,

179
00:07:23,781 --> 00:07:25,650
WHICH MAKES IT
EVEN MORE EMBARRASSING,

180
00:07:25,650 --> 00:07:26,951
BECAUSE SHE'S
A JUDGE ON PANEL.

181
00:07:26,951 --> 00:07:28,453
WHO IS
THE MOD?

182
00:07:28,453 --> 00:07:30,455
IT WAS SUPPOSED
TO BE ME, TWIGGY.

183
00:07:30,455 --> 00:07:32,357
OH, DEAR.
(laughs)

184
00:07:32,357 --> 00:07:34,492
DO YOU THINK MOD IS A LOOK
THAT ANY GIRL CAN DO?

185
00:07:34,492 --> 00:07:36,494
OH, ABSOLUTELY,
AND IT'S SO MUCH FUN.

186
00:07:36,494 --> 00:07:38,530
AND WHAT'S GREAT NOW--
OUT THERE

187
00:07:38,530 --> 00:07:39,964
THERE'S
ORIGINAL STUFF

188
00:07:39,964 --> 00:07:41,799
IF YOU CAN FORAGE
IN ALL THE SECOND-HAND SHOPS.

189
00:07:41,799 --> 00:07:44,235
YOU'VE GOT TO THINK
BIG BELL-BOTTOMS,

190
00:07:44,235 --> 00:07:45,603
MINI-MINI-MINI-SKIRT,

191
00:07:45,603 --> 00:07:47,539
TINY LITTLE
JUMPERS--

192
00:07:47,539 --> 00:07:49,207
FLATTEN YOUR CHEST
IF YOU CAN--

193
00:07:49,207 --> 00:07:51,309
AND TRY
AND COPY THAT.

194
00:07:51,309 --> 00:07:53,411
THAT'S
COMPLETELY '60s.

195
00:07:53,411 --> 00:07:54,779
THEY'D BETTER GET OUT
ON THE ROAD, HAVEN'T THEY?

196
00:07:54,779 --> 00:07:55,914
BETTER GET
ON THE ROAD.

197
00:07:55,914 --> 00:07:57,849
IT'S TIME TO HIT THE ROAD,
GIRLS.

198
00:07:57,849 --> 00:08:01,586
YOU'VE GOT FOUR GO-SEES
TO GO TO, EACH OF YOU--

199
00:08:01,586 --> 00:08:03,621
ASHLEY ISHAM,
BEN SHERMAN,

200
00:08:03,621 --> 00:08:06,291
PPQ,
ROBERT CARY-WILLIAMS.

201
00:08:06,291 --> 00:08:09,527
NOW, GIRLS, WHEN YOU GO
TO EACH OF THESE FOUR GO-SEES,

202
00:08:09,527 --> 00:08:12,330
YOU WILL HAVE TO DRESS
ACCORDING TO THEIR STYLES.

203
00:08:12,330 --> 00:08:15,600
SO WHEN YOU GO TO PPQ,
YOU SHOULD WEAR A MOD OUTFIT.

204
00:08:15,600 --> 00:08:17,335
WHEN YOU GO
TO ROBERT CARY-WILLIAMS,

205
00:08:17,335 --> 00:08:18,670
YOU SHOULD
DRESS PUNK.

206
00:08:18,670 --> 00:08:20,405
WHEN YOU GO
TO ASHLEY ISHAM,

207
00:08:20,405 --> 00:08:21,706
YOU SHOULD LOOK
BOLLYWOOD.

208
00:08:21,706 --> 00:08:23,875
AND TO BEN SHERMAN,
YOU SHOULD LOOK PREPPY.

209
00:08:23,875 --> 00:08:26,578
EACH DESIGNER THAT YOU GO
AND SEE IS GONNA EVALUATE YOU

210
00:08:26,578 --> 00:08:28,880
ON THE KNOWLEDGE
OF THEIR STYLE,

211
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:32,517
ON YOUR GENERAL APPEARANCE,
AND YOUR MODEL BOOK.

212
00:08:32,517 --> 00:08:33,918
NOW WE'RE NOT
SO MEAN

213
00:08:33,918 --> 00:08:35,687
THAT WE'D SEND YOU OFF
ON THESE GO-SEES

214
00:08:35,687 --> 00:08:37,455
WITH JUST
WHAT YOU'RE WEARING.

215
00:08:37,455 --> 00:08:39,224
YOU'RE GONNA HAVE
150 QUID,

216
00:08:39,224 --> 00:08:40,692
OR POUNDS,
AS THEY'RE KNOWN.

217
00:08:40,692 --> 00:08:42,327
GO INTO
SPITALFIELDS MARKET.

218
00:08:42,327 --> 00:08:43,528
BUY WHAT YOU CAN.

219
00:08:43,528 --> 00:08:45,263
GOOD LUCK.

220
00:08:45,263 --> 00:08:46,831
THE STAKES ON THIS CHALLENGE
ARE GREATER THAN EVER,

221
00:08:46,831 --> 00:08:48,633
BECAUSE THE WINNER
WILL RECEIVE

222
00:08:48,633 --> 00:08:51,302
100 FRAMES OF THIS WEEK'S
PHOTO SHOOT,

223
00:08:51,302 --> 00:08:53,504
AND WE ALL KNOW
THAT THE MORE FRAMES YOU HAVE,

224
00:08:53,504 --> 00:08:55,940
THE MORE CHANCES YOU'LL HAVE
TO IMPRESS US JUDGES LATER.

225
00:08:57,909 --> 00:08:58,910
MAPS.

226
00:08:58,910 --> 00:09:00,345
I THINK
ALL THE GIRLS

227
00:09:00,345 --> 00:09:02,347
WERE IN A LITTLE BIT
OF A PANIC ATTACK.

228
00:09:02,347 --> 00:09:03,548
DON'T GET LOST.

229
00:09:03,548 --> 00:09:05,216
I'M THINKING,
"OH, MY GOSH,"

230
00:09:05,216 --> 00:09:06,284
LIKE,
"WHAT AM I GONNA DO?"

231
00:09:06,284 --> 00:09:07,385
SO GET GOING.

232
00:09:12,924 --> 00:09:14,792
SPITALFIELD MARKET
IS JUST A LARGE FLEA MARKET

233
00:09:14,792 --> 00:09:17,929
THAT SELLS EVERYTHING
CHEAP.

234
00:09:18,830 --> 00:09:20,765
IT WOULD LOOK LIKE A DRESS,
RIGHT, A REALLY SHORT ONE?

235
00:09:20,765 --> 00:09:22,667
YEAH, BUT IT'S A,
LIKE A LONG SHIRT.

236
00:09:22,667 --> 00:09:24,302
I KNOW IT'S A SHIRT,
BUT...

237
00:09:24,302 --> 00:09:25,903
I CAN'T REALLY FIND
ANYTHING THAT I'M LOOKING FOR.

238
00:09:25,903 --> 00:09:27,939
♪♪♪

239
00:09:33,311 --> 00:09:34,879
WHAT'S THE SMALLEST SIZE
YOU HAVE IN THIS ONE?

240
00:09:34,879 --> 00:09:35,880
THAT'S A SMALL.

241
00:09:35,880 --> 00:09:36,914
- THIS ONE?
- YEAH.

242
00:09:36,914 --> 00:09:38,249
PUNK. PUNK.

243
00:09:38,249 --> 00:09:40,184
I CAN'T FIND NO PANTS
ANYWHERE IN HERE.

244
00:09:40,184 --> 00:09:42,320
THIS IS JUST NOT WORKING OUT
FOR ME.

245
00:09:42,320 --> 00:09:43,921
EVERYTHING
LOOKS BAD.

246
00:09:43,921 --> 00:09:45,823
I COULDN'T FIND ANYTHING
THAT I REALLY WANTED

247
00:09:45,823 --> 00:09:47,425
THAT I THOUGHT WOULD
FIT THE STYLES.

248
00:09:47,425 --> 00:09:49,427
SO I'M DEFINITELY GONNA
BE PRESSED

249
00:09:49,427 --> 00:09:51,462
AS FAR AS
THIS COMPETITION GOES.

250
00:09:51,462 --> 00:09:53,464
♪♪♪

251
00:09:53,464 --> 00:09:54,465
HOLD ON. HOLD ON.

252
00:09:58,736 --> 00:10:01,439
I DEFINITELY HAVE
FOUR OUTFITS,

253
00:10:01,439 --> 00:10:04,442
BUT I DON'T KNOW IF THEY'RE
COVERING ANY OF THE BASES

254
00:10:04,442 --> 00:10:07,312
OF THE STYLE THAT I'M SUPPOSED
TO BE COVERING.

255
00:10:09,414 --> 00:10:10,815
NO BIG DEAL TO GET DRESSED
IN THE CAR.

256
00:10:10,815 --> 00:10:12,317
YOU GOTTA DO
WHAT YOU GOTTA DO.

257
00:10:12,317 --> 00:10:13,551
I'M A LITTLE BIT CRUNCHED
FOR TIME,

258
00:10:13,551 --> 00:10:14,919
SO WE GOTTA
KEEP IT MOVING.

259
00:10:20,525 --> 00:10:22,827
♪♪♪

260
00:10:22,827 --> 00:10:24,329
WE HAVE A CHALLENGE,

261
00:10:24,329 --> 00:10:28,399
AND OUR CHALLENGE IS WE HAVE
TO GO ON FOUR GO-SEES.

262
00:10:28,399 --> 00:10:30,401
NOW IT'S JUST GETTING THERE
AND DOING A GOOD JOB

263
00:10:30,401 --> 00:10:31,436
AND GETTING THEM
ALL DONE.

264
00:10:31,436 --> 00:10:32,704
HELLO,
WHAT'S YOUR NAME?

265
00:10:32,704 --> 00:10:33,705
I'M JAYLA.

266
00:10:33,705 --> 00:10:34,939
JAYLA-- HI, JAYLA.
COME IN.

267
00:10:34,939 --> 00:10:36,474
OKAY, LET'S HAVE A LOOK
AT YOUR BOOK.

268
00:10:36,474 --> 00:10:38,209
OKAY.

269
00:10:38,209 --> 00:10:40,178
SO THE OUTFITS
THAT WE PICKED OUT TODAY

270
00:10:40,178 --> 00:10:42,714
ARE FROM WHAT WE CALL
OUR HERITAGE LINE.

271
00:10:42,714 --> 00:10:43,815
I THINK WE'LL GO
FOR THESE.

272
00:10:43,815 --> 00:10:48,286
THESE ARE A GREAT
SKINNY LEG JEANS, AND...

273
00:10:48,286 --> 00:10:50,521
SO THIS IS YOUR KIND OF, LIKE,
PREPPY LOOK

274
00:10:50,521 --> 00:10:51,656
THAT YOU'VE COME
TODAY?

275
00:10:51,656 --> 00:10:53,224
ALMOST NAVAL
THERE...

276
00:10:53,224 --> 00:10:54,225
NAVAL?

277
00:10:54,225 --> 00:10:54,859
...THERE
WITH YOUR STRIPED TOP.

278
00:10:54,859 --> 00:10:56,728
OH, NO!

279
00:10:56,728 --> 00:10:58,463
NOT PREPPY
AT ALL.

280
00:10:58,463 --> 00:10:59,731
NOT AT ALL
PREPPY.

281
00:10:59,731 --> 00:11:01,566
THE DESIGNER
AT BEN SHERMAN--

282
00:11:01,566 --> 00:11:03,234
SHE'S,
LIKE, STUCK UP.

283
00:11:04,936 --> 00:11:07,271
(sighs)
THAT'S AWFUL.

284
00:11:07,271 --> 00:11:09,974
♪♪♪

285
00:11:09,974 --> 00:11:11,409
HELLO.

286
00:11:11,409 --> 00:11:12,477
HI,
I'M PERCY.

287
00:11:12,477 --> 00:11:13,711
NICE TO MEET YOU.
I'M NIK.

288
00:11:13,711 --> 00:11:14,812
NIK,
HELLO.

289
00:11:14,812 --> 00:11:16,180
HI.

290
00:11:16,180 --> 00:11:17,682
DID YOU MAKE THIS?

291
00:11:17,682 --> 00:11:19,517
(giggles)

292
00:11:19,517 --> 00:11:20,618
UM, I DID NOT
MAKE IT.

293
00:11:20,618 --> 00:11:22,253
I JUST PICKED IT UP
AT A FLEA MARKET.

294
00:11:22,253 --> 00:11:23,921
I WAS TRYING TO GO
FOR THAT MOD APPEAL.

295
00:11:23,921 --> 00:11:25,923
MY FIRST IMPRESSION
OF NIK

296
00:11:25,923 --> 00:11:29,293
WAS THAT HER DRESS
WAS REALLY QUITE BOLD.

297
00:11:29,293 --> 00:11:30,595
TRYING TO ACHIEVE
A LOOK.

298
00:11:30,595 --> 00:11:32,296
SHE ASKED ME
ABOUT MY OUTFIT.

299
00:11:32,296 --> 00:11:34,298
I DON'T KNOW IF IT WAS
BECAUSE IT WAS RIDICULOUS

300
00:11:34,298 --> 00:11:35,366
OR SHE LIKED IT.

301
00:11:35,366 --> 00:11:36,768
♪♪♪

302
00:11:36,768 --> 00:11:38,436
HI, I'M BRE,
NICE TO MEET YOU.

303
00:11:38,436 --> 00:11:39,604
I'M ASHLEY ISHAM,
NICE TO MEET YOU.

304
00:11:42,306 --> 00:11:43,775
OH, MY GOODNESS,
I'M SO SORRY.

305
00:11:43,775 --> 00:11:44,776
I LEFT IT
IN MY CAR.

306
00:11:44,776 --> 00:11:45,777
OKAY,
NO PROBLEM.

307
00:11:45,777 --> 00:11:48,379
I LEFT
MY BOOK.

308
00:11:48,379 --> 00:11:50,281
I WAS ACTUALLY VERY SHOCKED
THAT BRE WOULD ACTUALLY COME

309
00:11:50,281 --> 00:11:53,317
TO A GO-SEE
WITHOUT A PORTFOLIO.

310
00:11:53,317 --> 00:11:54,685
THIS IS
MY MOST RECENT PICTURE.

311
00:11:54,685 --> 00:11:56,754
I ACTUALLY DID THAT ONE
IN LONDON.

312
00:11:56,754 --> 00:11:58,556
THAT'S
A VERY GOOD PICTURE.

313
00:11:58,556 --> 00:12:00,558
SHE HAS
AN INCREDIBLE FACE,

314
00:12:00,558 --> 00:12:02,560
BUT I THINK SHE NEEDS
A LITTLE BIT OF SELF-CONFIDENCE.

315
00:12:02,560 --> 00:12:03,561
HAVE A GOOD DAY.

316
00:12:03,561 --> 00:12:04,762
THANK YOU.
YOU TOO.

317
00:12:06,264 --> 00:12:08,232
I'M FAILING MISERABLY
AT MODELING.

318
00:12:08,232 --> 00:12:10,268
♪♪♪

319
00:12:10,268 --> 00:12:11,469
HI.

320
00:12:11,469 --> 00:12:12,336
HELLO.
HOW'S IT GOING?

321
00:12:12,336 --> 00:12:13,538
I'M NICOLE.

322
00:12:13,538 --> 00:12:15,540
SO YOU'VE DONE
THE PREPPY LOOK.

323
00:12:15,540 --> 00:12:17,542
YOU'RE DOING KIND OF
AVANT-GARDE FASHION THERE.

324
00:12:17,542 --> 00:12:19,544
I'M NOT REALLY FEELING
HER VIBE.

325
00:12:19,544 --> 00:12:21,512
I DON'T REALLY THINK THAT
SHE IS REALLY FEELING ME.

326
00:12:21,512 --> 00:12:23,681
NOT AT ALL
PREPPY.

327
00:12:23,681 --> 00:12:26,751
NOT BY ANY CONSCIOUS
INTERPRETATION OF PREPPY.

328
00:12:26,751 --> 00:12:28,953
♪♪♪

329
00:12:30,621 --> 00:12:33,257
THE THINGS I DO
FOR "ANTM."

330
00:12:34,425 --> 00:12:36,427
RIGHT-- STOP.

331
00:12:36,427 --> 00:12:37,528
WE'RE NOT GOING TO BE
DOING ANY OF THIS--

332
00:12:37,528 --> 00:12:39,197
THIS--
THIS THING.

333
00:12:39,197 --> 00:12:40,665
SO, OF COURSE, I DO
MY SIGNATURE WALK,

334
00:12:40,665 --> 00:12:42,467
AND HE TELLS ME,
"STOP."

335
00:12:42,467 --> 00:12:43,868
WE'VE BEEN SEEING THAT
ALL OVER THE BLOODY PLACE.

336
00:12:43,868 --> 00:12:45,736
UNH-UNH,
NO WAY.

337
00:12:45,736 --> 00:12:48,206
OKAY, THAT'S MORE
LIKE IT.

338
00:12:48,206 --> 00:12:49,874
THAT'S IT. PERFECT.
EXCELLENT.

339
00:12:49,874 --> 00:12:52,310
♪♪♪

340
00:12:52,310 --> 00:12:53,311
HI.

341
00:12:53,311 --> 00:12:54,479
HELLO.

342
00:12:54,479 --> 00:12:56,614
GOOD AFTERNOON TO YOU,
I'M ASHLEY.

343
00:12:56,614 --> 00:12:59,283
NIK-- THE WAY SHE PUT HER
COLORS TOGETHER ARE FANTASTIC.

344
00:12:59,283 --> 00:13:01,486
♪♪♪

345
00:13:01,486 --> 00:13:03,454
THANK YOU
VERY MUCH.

346
00:13:03,454 --> 00:13:04,489
THANK YOU.

347
00:13:04,489 --> 00:13:07,892
♪♪♪

348
00:13:10,261 --> 00:13:12,497
WE'RE GOING TO DO
TWO DIFFERENT LOOKS FOR YOU.

349
00:13:12,497 --> 00:13:15,266
SO WE'RE TRYING TO DO
AN ENGLISH PUNK LOOK,

350
00:13:15,266 --> 00:13:16,868
AND THAT'S MORE OF
A COUTURE PIECE.

351
00:13:16,868 --> 00:13:18,369
PERFECT.

352
00:13:18,369 --> 00:13:19,370
EXCELLENT, EXCELLENT.

353
00:13:19,370 --> 00:13:20,738
THAT'S GOOD.

354
00:13:20,738 --> 00:13:22,273
I'M NOT REALLY LIKE
THAT PUNK OF A PERSON,

355
00:13:22,273 --> 00:13:23,708
BUT I JUST,
LIKE, FELT THE OUTFIT

356
00:13:23,708 --> 00:13:25,309
AND KINDA WENT
WITH IT,

357
00:13:25,309 --> 00:13:26,777
AND HE REALLY LIKED
MY WALK,

358
00:13:26,777 --> 00:13:28,212
SO I WAS HAPPY
ABOUT THAT, DEFINITELY.

359
00:13:28,546 --> 00:13:31,282
♪♪♪

360
00:13:31,282 --> 00:13:33,284
I REALLY, YOU KNOW,
NEED TO STEP UP THINGS,

361
00:13:33,284 --> 00:13:35,686
BECAUSE I THINK THAT
THERE COULD BE

362
00:13:35,686 --> 00:13:37,688
ANOTHER CHANCE
THAT I'M GOING HOME.

363
00:13:37,688 --> 00:13:39,757
I LIKE THE WAY
YOU PUT THINGS TOGETHER.

364
00:13:39,757 --> 00:13:40,825
HAVE YOU GOT
A PAIR OF SHOES?

365
00:13:40,825 --> 00:13:41,893
THESE ARE THE ONLY ONES
I BROUGHT.

366
00:13:41,893 --> 00:13:43,561
AHH.

367
00:13:43,561 --> 00:13:45,663
I CAN'T BELIEVE THAT JAYLA
AS A PROFESSIONAL MODEL

368
00:13:45,663 --> 00:13:47,398
WOULDN'T BRING HER OWN
HIGH HEELS.

369
00:13:47,398 --> 00:13:48,399
COULD WE SEE
YOUR WALK?

370
00:13:48,399 --> 00:13:49,200
SURE.

371
00:13:53,271 --> 00:13:53,638
VERY NICE.

372
00:13:53,638 --> 00:13:54,906
THANK YOU
VERY MUCH.

373
00:13:54,906 --> 00:13:56,941
I FIND THAT JAYLA'S
JUST TOO STIFF,

374
00:13:56,941 --> 00:13:59,410
AND I THINK THAT SHE STILL
NEEDS TO WORK ON THAT WALK.

375
00:14:02,513 --> 00:14:06,284
AND TODAY,
NO ONE WON THE CHALLENGE.

376
00:14:06,284 --> 00:14:09,720
TODAY,
YOU ALL ARE FAILURES.

377
00:14:09,720 --> 00:14:11,589
HELLO, LADIES,
WELCOME BACK.

378
00:14:11,589 --> 00:14:15,226
I HAVE THE EVALUATION SHEETS
FROM EVERY DESIGNER,

379
00:14:15,226 --> 00:14:18,563
AND IT'S TIME
FOR YOUR INDIVIDUAL CRITIQUE.

380
00:14:18,563 --> 00:14:20,831
NICOLE,
YOU LOOK THE BEST.

381
00:14:20,831 --> 00:14:23,534
NIK, YOU ARE THE MOST
PROFESSIONAL.

382
00:14:23,534 --> 00:14:24,902
JAYLA...

383
00:14:24,902 --> 00:14:26,804
I'D SAY THAT I HAVE
A PRETTY DECENT WALK.

384
00:14:26,804 --> 00:14:30,274
YOU ARE THE WORST RUNWAY WALKER
OVERALL.

385
00:14:30,274 --> 00:14:34,412
BRE, YOUR GENERAL APPEARANCE
WAS LEAST APPRECIATED.

386
00:14:34,412 --> 00:14:36,547
YOUR PHOTOS
ARE NOT STRONG,

387
00:14:36,547 --> 00:14:40,518
BUT YOU ARE VERY, VERY GOOD
AT TAKING DIRECTION.

388
00:14:40,518 --> 00:14:41,919
I CANNOT
DRESS,

389
00:14:41,919 --> 00:14:43,754
BUT, OH, OH, OH--

390
00:14:43,754 --> 00:14:46,557
I TAKE
GOOD DIRECTION.

391
00:14:46,557 --> 00:14:50,628
ALL FOUR DESIGNERS
UNANIMOUSLY AGREED THAT,

392
00:14:50,628 --> 00:14:52,763
NIK,
YOU ARE THE WINNER.

393
00:14:52,763 --> 00:14:53,831
THANK YOU
SO MUCH.

394
00:14:53,831 --> 00:14:54,966
YOU'RE WELCOME.

395
00:14:54,966 --> 00:14:56,434
SINCE YOU'VE WON,

396
00:14:56,434 --> 00:14:59,270
YOU ARE GOING
TO GET A HUNDRED FRAMES

397
00:14:59,270 --> 00:15:01,372
FOR A PHOTO SHOOT
TOMORROW,

398
00:15:01,372 --> 00:15:05,710
AND YOU'VE GOT
TO CHOOSE A FRIEND.

399
00:15:05,710 --> 00:15:07,278
I'M GOING
TO CHOOSE NICOLE.

400
00:15:07,278 --> 00:15:10,581
NICOLE, YOU ARE GOING
TO GET 80 FRAMES.

401
00:15:10,581 --> 00:15:12,783
I'M THINKING THAT OBVIOUSLY
THE MORE FRAMES YOU GET,

402
00:15:12,783 --> 00:15:14,852
THE MORE OF AN ADVANTAGE
YOU HAVE.

403
00:15:14,852 --> 00:15:16,253
AS ANOTHER
SURPRISE,

404
00:15:16,253 --> 00:15:21,959
YOU GET TO PICK
A FRIEND AS WELL.

405
00:15:21,959 --> 00:15:24,228
I'LL TAKE
JAYLA.

406
00:15:24,228 --> 00:15:25,763
I GET TO PICK
SOMEONE ELSE.

407
00:15:25,763 --> 00:15:27,832
I HATE BRE, SO OBVIOUSLY
I GRABBED JAYLA.

408
00:15:27,832 --> 00:15:30,568
JAYLA,
YOU GET 60 FRAMES.

409
00:15:30,568 --> 00:15:32,637
LAST, BUT NOT LEAST,
BRE,

410
00:15:32,637 --> 00:15:34,205
- YOU WILL GET...
- FIVE FRAMES.

411
00:15:34,205 --> 00:15:38,976
50 FRAMES, BUT YOU
WILL HAVE TO GO FIRST,

412
00:15:38,976 --> 00:15:41,445
AND YOU CANNOT SEE YOURSELF
IN A MIRROR

413
00:15:41,445 --> 00:15:43,214
PRIOR TO
THE PHOTO SHOOT, OKAY?

414
00:15:43,214 --> 00:15:44,215
I GUESS.

415
00:15:44,215 --> 00:15:45,683
(laughing)

416
00:15:45,683 --> 00:15:48,719
I GET 50 FRAMES AND, OH,
LIFE ONLY GETS BETTER.

417
00:15:48,719 --> 00:15:51,455
I'M NOT ALLOWED TO SEE MYSELF
AFTER I GET MY MAKEUP DONE.

418
00:15:51,455 --> 00:15:52,823
NICE TO MEET
YOU, GIRLS.

419
00:15:52,823 --> 00:15:54,525
BYE!

420
00:15:54,525 --> 00:15:56,961
THEN BRE FINDS OUT
THAT SHE CAN'T LOOK AT HERSELF

421
00:15:56,961 --> 00:15:59,530
IN THE MIRROR BEFORE SHE GOES
ON HER PHOTO SHOOT.

422
00:15:59,530 --> 00:16:02,333
UM...
WHATEVER.

423
00:16:02,333 --> 00:16:04,769
♪♪♪

424
00:16:04,769 --> 00:16:08,606
CAN YOU BUCKLE THAT
FOR ME?

425
00:16:08,606 --> 00:16:09,774
THE TIGHTEST ONE?

426
00:16:09,774 --> 00:16:11,242
NIK HAS NEVER
WRONGED ME,

427
00:16:11,242 --> 00:16:12,610
AND IN FACT,

428
00:16:12,610 --> 00:16:17,181
NIK HAS BEEN PRETTY MUCH
SIDE BY SIDE WITH ME,

429
00:16:17,181 --> 00:16:19,183
YOU KNOW, SINCE WE
CAME OUT TO LONDON.

430
00:16:24,522 --> 00:16:27,224
WITH THE WHOLE
RED BULL SCENARIO

431
00:16:27,224 --> 00:16:29,360
AND THE RED BULL
STORY,

432
00:16:29,360 --> 00:16:31,328
I DON'T EVEN KNOW
WHY IT WAS DONE.

433
00:16:31,328 --> 00:16:33,230
I THINK IT WAS CHILDISH
AND I THINK IT WAS ALSO EVIL.

434
00:16:33,230 --> 00:16:34,398
WHERE'S YOUR STUFF
AT?

435
00:16:34,398 --> 00:16:35,533
YOU DRANK IT.
YOU STOLE IT.

436
00:16:35,533 --> 00:16:37,201
THAT'S STEALING, BRE.

437
00:16:37,201 --> 00:16:38,402
YOUR RED BULLS
ARE GONE.

438
00:16:38,402 --> 00:16:39,737
SO IS
MY GRANOLA.

439
00:16:39,737 --> 00:16:41,405
WHAT DO YOU WANT ME
TO DO NOW?

440
00:16:41,405 --> 00:16:44,375
EVEN THOUGH IT LOOKS LIKE
ME AND BRE ARE EXTREMELY CLOSE,

441
00:16:44,375 --> 00:16:48,412
I KNOW THAT SHE IS SUPPOSEDLY
"KEEPING" HER ENEMIES CLOSE,

442
00:16:48,412 --> 00:16:49,747
AND WHAT DO YOU THINK
I'M DOING?

443
00:16:49,747 --> 00:16:52,883
♪♪♪

444
00:16:54,618 --> 00:16:55,953
TODAY WE WAKE UP
AND WE'RE TOLD

445
00:16:55,953 --> 00:16:57,955
THAT WE'RE GONNA PAIR UP
INTO TWO GROUPS

446
00:16:57,955 --> 00:16:59,223
AND GO SEE
LONDON.

447
00:17:03,828 --> 00:17:05,629
BRE AND NICOLE ARE,
YOU KNOW,

448
00:17:05,629 --> 00:17:07,832
REALLY, REALLY PISSED OFF
AT EACH OTHER,

449
00:17:07,832 --> 00:17:08,799
AND ME AND NIK
ARE STUCK IN THE MIDDLE.

450
00:17:11,234 --> 00:17:12,435
YEAH.

451
00:17:12,435 --> 00:17:14,438
NO DRAMA,
NO ARGUING.

452
00:17:14,438 --> 00:17:15,705
SAY ONE OF US GOES OUT
WITH NICOLE,

453
00:17:15,705 --> 00:17:17,308
ONE OF US GOES OUT
WITH BRE,

454
00:17:17,308 --> 00:17:19,777
ALL WE'RE GONNA HEAR
IS STUFF ABOUT THE OTHER PERSON.

455
00:17:21,712 --> 00:17:23,280
THE GROUP
IS SO SMALL.

456
00:17:23,280 --> 00:17:25,883
NO ONE NEEDS TO HAVE THE DRAMA
AND THE STRESS FACTOR.

457
00:17:25,883 --> 00:17:27,651
I DON'T WANT TO SPLIT
YOU AND JAYLA UP,

458
00:17:27,651 --> 00:17:28,919
BUT YOU KNOW
THE SITUATION.

459
00:17:28,919 --> 00:17:31,722
I'M SORRY, ME AND NIK
WANT TO GO TOGETHER.

460
00:17:34,290 --> 00:17:36,293
ARE YOU
SERIOUS?

461
00:17:36,293 --> 00:17:37,495
OH,
MY GOODNESS.

462
00:17:37,495 --> 00:17:38,796
DON'T LOOK AT ME,
NICOLE.

463
00:17:38,796 --> 00:17:39,864
YOU KNOW
THAT'S WACK.

464
00:17:48,272 --> 00:17:50,207
♪♪

465
00:17:50,207 --> 00:17:51,242
TODAY WE WAKE UP,

466
00:17:51,242 --> 00:17:54,211
AND WE'RE TOLD THAT WE'RE
GONNA PAIR UP INTO TWO GROUPS

467
00:17:54,211 --> 00:17:55,579
AND GO SEE LONDON.

468
00:17:55,579 --> 00:17:58,249
I'M SORRY, ME AND NIK
WANT TO GO TOGETHER.

469
00:17:58,249 --> 00:17:59,817
ARE YOU SERIOUS?

470
00:17:59,817 --> 00:18:02,419
BRE AND I
GET STUCK TOGETHER.

471
00:18:02,419 --> 00:18:04,255
I DON'T REALLY WANT
TO BE WITH HER.

472
00:18:05,656 --> 00:18:08,225
NICOLE-- I KNOW SHE IS
NOT LOOKING FORWARD

473
00:18:08,225 --> 00:18:09,960
TO EVEN
BREATHING NEXT TO ME.

474
00:18:16,300 --> 00:18:18,602
I HAD PROBLEMS WITH YOU
IN THE BEGINNING,

475
00:18:18,602 --> 00:18:21,806
AND-- I MEAN,
I GOT OVER THAT.

476
00:18:21,806 --> 00:18:23,507
I JUST WANTED TO SAY THAT
BEFORE YOU STARTED HITTING ME.

477
00:18:23,507 --> 00:18:25,709
...THERE'S ONE PERSON
IN THIS HOUSE

478
00:18:25,709 --> 00:18:27,578
THAT I SEVERELY,
SEVERELY DISLIKE

479
00:18:27,578 --> 00:18:28,879
ON THE BORDERLINE
OF HATE.

480
00:18:28,879 --> 00:18:30,781
THAT'S NIK.

481
00:18:30,781 --> 00:18:33,651
THE ONE THING THAT I REALLY,
REALLY HOPE HAPPENS RIGHT NOW

482
00:18:33,651 --> 00:18:35,920
IS THAT SHE KEEPS THE SAME
STUPID FACIAL EXPRESSION

483
00:18:35,920 --> 00:18:37,555
IN ALL
HER PICTURES.

484
00:18:37,555 --> 00:18:38,622
THAT WAY, THEY'RE LIKE,
"HMM. YEAH. THAT'S RIGHT.

485
00:18:38,622 --> 00:18:39,890
YOU SUCK.
BYE-BYE."

486
00:18:39,890 --> 00:18:41,625
NO, IT'S OKAY.

487
00:18:41,625 --> 00:18:43,794
ALL I CAN SAY IS I DID NOT
COME HERE TO MAKE FRIENDS,

488
00:18:43,794 --> 00:18:45,396
AND I DIDN'T COME HERE
TO MAKE ENEMIES.

489
00:18:45,396 --> 00:18:47,331
I CAME HERE
FOR AN OPPORTUNITY

490
00:18:47,331 --> 00:18:49,533
AND, YOU KNOW,
THAT'S LIFE.

491
00:18:49,533 --> 00:18:52,303
IT'S A DIRTY WORLD,
YOU KNOW?

492
00:18:52,303 --> 00:18:53,637
AND EVERYONE'S HERE
FOR THEMSELVES.

493
00:18:53,637 --> 00:18:56,473
WHEN ME AND JAYLA GO ON OUR WALK
AROUND LONDON,

494
00:18:56,473 --> 00:18:58,275
SHE JUST WANTED
TO KINDA CLEAR THINGS UP,

495
00:18:58,275 --> 00:18:59,543
AND IT'S
KINDA NICE.

496
00:18:59,543 --> 00:19:01,812
IT DOES KINDA SHOW THAT
SHE'S MATURE IN THAT SENSE.

497
00:19:04,748 --> 00:19:05,916
I'M SURE BRE IS
A LITTLE BIT NERVOUS

498
00:19:05,916 --> 00:19:09,854
ABOUT GOING ON THIS WALK
WITH ME.

499
00:19:09,854 --> 00:19:11,822
BUT I DON'T THINK SHE WANTS
ANY MORE DRAMA.

500
00:19:11,822 --> 00:19:14,391
SHE'S MADE TOO MUCH
OF A FOOL OF HERSELF ALREADY.

501
00:19:14,391 --> 00:19:17,695
IS THERE SOMEWHERE WE COULD STOP
AND GET, LIKE, SOME WINE?

502
00:19:17,695 --> 00:19:20,831
OH, THAT WOULD BE
VERY NICE.

503
00:19:20,831 --> 00:19:22,266
IT SOUNDED SO STUPID.

504
00:19:22,266 --> 00:19:23,801
LIKE, WE WERE ARGUING OVER
ENERGY DRINKS.

505
00:19:23,801 --> 00:19:25,669
THE SITUATION JUST WENT
OUT OF CONTROL.

506
00:19:25,669 --> 00:19:28,272
I WAS WRONG.

507
00:19:28,272 --> 00:19:29,506
IF THE SHOE WAS
ON THE OTHER FOOT,

508
00:19:29,506 --> 00:19:31,342
AND YOU DID THAT
TO ME,

509
00:19:31,342 --> 00:19:34,211
I WOULDN'T HAVE REACTED
ANY DIFFERENTLY THAN YOU WOULD,

510
00:19:34,211 --> 00:19:35,713
AND I PROBABLY WOULDN'T EVEN
BE TALKING RIGHT NOW.

511
00:19:35,713 --> 00:19:37,514
I'D BE SO HURT.

512
00:19:37,514 --> 00:19:39,950
BUT THAT JUST SHOWS THAT
YOU'RE MATURE,

513
00:19:39,950 --> 00:19:41,652
AND I WAS BEING
SO STUPID AND IMMATURE

514
00:19:41,652 --> 00:19:43,387
ABOUT THE SITUATION.

515
00:19:43,387 --> 00:19:45,623
AND I WAS JUST WORKING OFF OF,
LIKE, ANGER AND EMOTIONS

516
00:19:45,623 --> 00:19:47,892
INSTEAD
OF THINKING LOGICALLY.

517
00:19:47,892 --> 00:19:50,261
SO...

518
00:19:50,261 --> 00:19:51,662
WELL,
WHAT'S DONE IS DONE.

519
00:19:51,662 --> 00:19:53,364
BUT I'LL BUY YOU
A WHOLE BUNCH OF RED BULL,

520
00:19:53,364 --> 00:19:55,566
AND I'LL PUT RIBBONS AND BOWS
ON THEM, OKAY?

521
00:19:55,566 --> 00:19:56,967
I'M ACTUALLY
REALLY GLAD THAT

522
00:19:56,967 --> 00:19:59,870
ME AND BRE ENDED UP
GOING OUT TOGETHER BECAUSE

523
00:19:59,870 --> 00:20:01,505
I DON'T WANT TO LIVE
WITH SOMEONE

524
00:20:01,505 --> 00:20:04,241
WHO I HAVE
THIS, YOU KNOW, DRAMA WITH.

525
00:20:07,912 --> 00:20:09,847
OH,
I HAD A GOOD DAY.

526
00:20:09,847 --> 00:20:10,748
I REALLY HAD
A GOOD DAY.

527
00:20:10,748 --> 00:20:11,382
SO DID I.

528
00:20:11,382 --> 00:20:15,185
I'M GLAD THAT WE ENDED UP
WALKING AROUND AND STUFF

529
00:20:15,185 --> 00:20:17,955
IN LONDON BECAUSE I THINK
WE NEEDED THAT,

530
00:20:17,955 --> 00:20:20,324
AND IT DEFINITELY MADE ME
OPEN UP

531
00:20:20,324 --> 00:20:21,425
AND SAY SOME THINGS
TO HER,

532
00:20:21,425 --> 00:20:23,761
ESPECIALLY LIKE,
"I'M SORRY."

533
00:20:23,761 --> 00:20:25,195
I DON'T WANT
ANY MORE DRAMA.

534
00:20:25,195 --> 00:20:25,930
NEITHER DO I.

535
00:20:28,432 --> 00:20:32,369
I'M REALLY GLAD THAT ME AND BRE
WENT TOGETHER, ACTUALLY.

536
00:20:32,369 --> 00:20:33,904
LIKE, WE HAD A GOOD TIME
AND WE GOT OVER OUR DIFFERENCES.

537
00:20:44,448 --> 00:20:46,850
TYRA MAIL.

538
00:20:46,850 --> 00:20:48,719
"YOU NEVER KNOW
WHO'LL BE JUDGING YOU.

539
00:20:48,719 --> 00:20:50,487
WILL YOU BE SARI
TOMORROW?"

540
00:20:50,487 --> 00:20:53,357
S-A-R-I. HMM.

541
00:20:53,357 --> 00:20:55,292
I HAVE NO IDEA WHAT IT MEANS
AS ALWAYS.

542
00:21:04,702 --> 00:21:07,237
I'M DREADING TODAY
BECAUSE I HAVE A PHOTO SHOOT.

543
00:21:07,237 --> 00:21:08,772
ON TOP OF THAT,
I DON'T FEEL GOOD.

544
00:21:08,772 --> 00:21:12,843
I HAVE A FEVER
AND A MIGRAINE.

545
00:21:12,843 --> 00:21:14,445
IT DON'T GET NO WORSE
THAN THIS.

546
00:21:17,281 --> 00:21:18,549
I'M SO HOT.

547
00:21:18,549 --> 00:21:20,451
I HAVE A FEVER.
I HAVE CRAMPS.

548
00:21:26,857 --> 00:21:28,425
JAYLA HAD GIVEN ME
SOME MEDICINE,

549
00:21:28,425 --> 00:21:31,528
AND THE MEDICINE
MAKES ME SUPER DROWSY

550
00:21:31,528 --> 00:21:33,530
AND ACTUALLY MAKES
MY MIGRAINE WORSE.

551
00:21:33,530 --> 00:21:34,631
IN HERE, GUYS.

552
00:21:36,667 --> 00:21:38,335
- HEY.
- HELLO.

553
00:21:38,335 --> 00:21:39,770
ALL RIGHT,

554
00:21:39,770 --> 00:21:42,206
SO YOU GIRLS OBVIOUSLY HAVE
HEARD ABOUT BOLLYWOOD, RIGHT?

555
00:21:42,206 --> 00:21:44,975
BOLLYWOOD FILMS ARE KNOWN TO BE
LARGER THAN LIFE.

556
00:21:44,975 --> 00:21:46,543
YOU KNOW,
ORNATE COSTUMES,

557
00:21:46,543 --> 00:21:47,745
LOTS OF COLOR.

558
00:21:47,745 --> 00:21:49,346
THAT'S WHAT YOU GUYS ARE
GONNA DO TODAY--

559
00:21:49,346 --> 00:21:51,849
A BOLLYWOOD-STYLE
INSPIRED PHOTO SHOOT.

560
00:21:51,849 --> 00:21:53,684
THERE'S GONNA BE
LOTS OF PEOPLE.

561
00:21:53,684 --> 00:21:55,586
SO THE REAL CHALLENGE HERE
TODAY IS

562
00:21:55,586 --> 00:21:57,488
CAN YOU STAND OUT
IN THE CROWD?

563
00:21:57,488 --> 00:21:59,757
ARE YOU GONNA BRING YOUR FACE
TO THE FOREFRONT

564
00:21:59,757 --> 00:22:01,325
AND BE NOTICED?

565
00:22:01,325 --> 00:22:03,193
OR ARE YOU GONNA
FADE INTO THE BACKGROUND?

566
00:22:03,193 --> 00:22:05,396
NOW YOU GUYS HAD A CHALLENGE
THE OTHER DAY-- WHO WON IT?

567
00:22:05,396 --> 00:22:06,697
NIK.

568
00:22:06,697 --> 00:22:09,666
ALL RIGHT, SO, NIK, YOU
ACTUALLY GET TO GO LAST TODAY,

569
00:22:09,666 --> 00:22:10,968
AND YOU HAVE
A HUNDRED FRAMES,

570
00:22:10,968 --> 00:22:12,403
WHICH MEANS
YOU CAN GET TO SEE

571
00:22:12,403 --> 00:22:13,871
WHAT THE OTHER THREE GIRLS
HAVE DONE

572
00:22:13,871 --> 00:22:15,406
AND YOU GET TO LEARN
FROM IT.

573
00:22:15,406 --> 00:22:16,940
NICOLE,
YOU GET TO GO SECOND LAST.

574
00:22:16,940 --> 00:22:18,375
YOU HAVE
80 FRAMES.

575
00:22:18,375 --> 00:22:20,611
JAYLA, YOU GET TO HAVE
60 FRAMES,

576
00:22:20,611 --> 00:22:22,346
AND YOU GET
TO GO SECOND.

577
00:22:22,346 --> 00:22:23,947
BUT, BRE,
YOU GET TO GO FIRST,

578
00:22:23,947 --> 00:22:25,883
AND YOU'RE
NOT GOING TO GET AN OPPORTUNITY

579
00:22:25,883 --> 00:22:27,384
TO LOOK
AT YOURSELF

580
00:22:27,384 --> 00:22:29,319
AFTER YOU'VE
COME OUT OF HAIR AND MAKEUP.

581
00:22:29,319 --> 00:22:32,256
SO YOU'VE KINDA GOT EVERYTHING
FIGHTING AGAINST YOU TODAY.

582
00:22:32,256 --> 00:22:35,192
NOW YOUR PHOTOGRAPHER
IS SOMEONE THAT YOU MAY KNOW.

583
00:22:35,192 --> 00:22:38,362
BUT WHAT YOU DON'T KNOW IS
THE PERSONAL REASON BEHIND

584
00:22:38,362 --> 00:22:41,965
WHY HE WANTED TO DO
THIS PHOTO SHOOT, ALL RIGHT?

585
00:22:41,965 --> 00:22:43,500
COME ON OUT,
NIGEL.

586
00:22:43,500 --> 00:22:44,301
HI, LADIES.

587
00:22:44,301 --> 00:22:45,536
HI!

588
00:22:45,536 --> 00:22:46,537
HOW ARE YOU?

589
00:22:46,537 --> 00:22:47,538
WAIT, WAIT, WAIT, WAIT.

590
00:22:47,538 --> 00:22:48,539
SURPRISE.

591
00:22:48,539 --> 00:22:50,507
- THIS IS NOT RIGHT.
- WELL, I KNOW.

592
00:22:50,507 --> 00:22:52,910
YOU WERE SUPPOSED TO DO
THE WHOLE BOLLYWOOD THING--

593
00:22:52,910 --> 00:22:53,977
HE'S BEEN WAITING
TO UNDRESS ME FOR DAYS.

594
00:22:53,977 --> 00:22:55,245
YEAH, EXACTLY.
THERE YOU GO.

595
00:22:55,245 --> 00:22:56,346
THERE'S
THE BOLLYWOOD THING.

596
00:22:56,346 --> 00:22:57,948
ANYWAY,
GOOD TO SEE YOU.

597
00:22:57,948 --> 00:22:59,583
FINALLY WE GET
TO WORK TOGETHER.

598
00:22:59,583 --> 00:23:00,818
I'M HALF
SRI LANKAN.

599
00:23:00,818 --> 00:23:02,519
MY MOTHER
IS SRI LANKAN.

600
00:23:02,519 --> 00:23:03,821
MY FATHER IS ENGLISH.

601
00:23:03,821 --> 00:23:05,456
SO THE WHOLE
BOLLYWOOD THEME

602
00:23:05,456 --> 00:23:07,658
AND WHAT INDIA MEANS
TO ENGLAND

603
00:23:07,658 --> 00:23:09,660
IS VERY SORT OF DEEP
IN MY HEART.

604
00:23:09,660 --> 00:23:11,261
I'M A LITTLE NERVOUS
AT FIRST,

605
00:23:11,261 --> 00:23:12,896
BECAUSE NIGEL
IS A JUDGE ON PANEL.

606
00:23:12,896 --> 00:23:16,366
AND IF YOU IMPRESS NIGEL,
IT COULD BE AN AMAZING THING.

607
00:23:16,366 --> 00:23:19,603
BUT IF YOU DON'T, IT COULD BE
A VERY DAMAGING SITUATION.

608
00:23:19,603 --> 00:23:21,605
♪♪♪

609
00:23:26,977 --> 00:23:28,512
BABY,
ARE YOU NOT FEELING GOOD?

610
00:23:28,512 --> 00:23:29,780
ARE YOU SICK?

611
00:23:29,780 --> 00:23:31,215
I DON'T WANT
TO HEAR IT.

612
00:23:31,215 --> 00:23:32,549
YOU HAVE TO PRETEND
TO BE HEALTHY.

613
00:23:32,549 --> 00:23:33,717
I DON'T
FEEL GOOD.

614
00:23:33,717 --> 00:23:34,818
YOU DON'T FEEL
GOOD?

615
00:23:34,818 --> 00:23:36,320
UNH-UNH.

616
00:23:36,320 --> 00:23:37,888
WHAT DO YOU MEAN,
LIKE YOU GOT A COLD?

617
00:23:37,888 --> 00:23:39,790
I KEEP GETTING FEVERS
AND MIGRAINES.

618
00:23:39,790 --> 00:23:41,792
DID YOU TAKE ANYTHING
FOR YOUR HEADACHE TODAY?

619
00:23:41,792 --> 00:23:43,594
JAYLA GAVE ME SOME BENADRYL,
AND THAT'S ABOUT IT.

620
00:23:43,594 --> 00:23:44,661
BENADRYL?

621
00:23:44,661 --> 00:23:46,263
AND
SOME TYLENOL PM.

622
00:23:46,263 --> 00:23:47,631
WHOEVER GAVE HER
THAT BENADRYL

623
00:23:47,631 --> 00:23:49,366
IS TRYING
TO SCREW HER UP,

624
00:23:49,366 --> 00:23:51,969
BECAUSE SHE IS SO DRAGGY
TODAY AND EXHAUSTED.

625
00:23:51,969 --> 00:23:54,404
YOU SAVE ALL THAT ENERGY
SO WHEN YOU ARE ON SET,

626
00:23:54,404 --> 00:23:56,306
WOW! POW!
IT ALL GOES.

627
00:23:56,306 --> 00:23:58,709
THEN YOU CAN FADE
AND DIE AFTERWARDS, YOU KNOW?

628
00:23:58,709 --> 00:24:00,477
I'M NOT REALLY
FEELING WELL TODAY.

629
00:24:00,477 --> 00:24:02,212
JUST SO HAPPENS THAT
I WOULD ONLY HAVE

630
00:24:02,212 --> 00:24:04,248
50 FRAMES
AT MY PHOTO SHOOT.

631
00:24:04,248 --> 00:24:05,916
I'M NOT ALLOWED
TO LOOK AT MYSELF,

632
00:24:05,916 --> 00:24:08,352
SO I HAVE
NO CLUE WHAT I LOOK LIKE.

633
00:24:08,352 --> 00:24:09,887
REALLY CONCENTRATE
ON THE CAMERA.

634
00:24:09,887 --> 00:24:12,623
WHAT IT IS-- I'M TRYING TO GET
YOU TO REALLY POP FROM WITHIN.

635
00:24:12,623 --> 00:24:16,693
KEEP IN MIND, AGAIN,
YOU ONLY HAVE 50 FRAMES.

636
00:24:16,693 --> 00:24:18,862
KEEP THE FINGERS
LIKE THAT.

637
00:24:18,862 --> 00:24:20,330
EYES TO ME,
EVERYBODY.

638
00:24:20,330 --> 00:24:22,699
LET'S MAKE
BOLLYWOOD HAPPY.

639
00:24:22,699 --> 00:24:23,867
NOW YOU'RE DOING A BIT
OF A TEAPOT THERE.

640
00:24:23,867 --> 00:24:25,269
THAT'S GOOD.

641
00:24:25,269 --> 00:24:26,603
IF BRE HAD WON
THE CHALLENGE,

642
00:24:26,603 --> 00:24:28,739
SHE COULD HAVE USED
THOSE EXTRA 50 FRAMES.

643
00:24:28,739 --> 00:24:29,940
COME ON,
MAKE ME PROUD.

644
00:24:29,940 --> 00:24:31,642
EYES TO ME, BRE,
ALWAYS.

645
00:24:31,642 --> 00:24:32,910
LAST FRAME,
BRE.

646
00:24:32,910 --> 00:24:34,711
REALLY CONCENTRATE,
EVERYBODY.

647
00:24:34,711 --> 00:24:36,246
THANK YOU
VERY MUCH.

648
00:24:36,246 --> 00:24:39,183
WHOO!
SHOT ONE DOWN!

649
00:24:39,183 --> 00:24:40,617
IT WAS KIND OF HARD
DEALING WITH THE FACT THAT

650
00:24:40,617 --> 00:24:42,753
I COULDN'T GET AS MANY FRAMES
AS THE OTHER GIRLS

651
00:24:42,753 --> 00:24:45,255
AND THAT
I COULDN'T SEE MYSELF.

652
00:24:45,255 --> 00:24:46,657
BRE WAS
NOT HERE TODAY.

653
00:24:46,657 --> 00:24:48,392
BRE LEFT
THE BUILDING.

654
00:24:48,392 --> 00:24:49,726
ACTUALLY, I DON'T THINK BRE
ENTERED THE BUILDING.

655
00:24:49,726 --> 00:24:51,228
OKAY, GUYS.
EVERYBODY FOCUS.

656
00:24:55,566 --> 00:24:57,801
JAYLA, JUST RELAX THE MOUTH
A LITTLE BIT LIKE THAT.

657
00:24:57,801 --> 00:24:58,802
AND JUST CHIN DOWN

658
00:24:58,802 --> 00:25:00,270
AND NOW EYES
TO ME.

659
00:25:00,270 --> 00:25:01,605
REALLY OOZE
WITH YOUR EYES.

660
00:25:01,605 --> 00:25:02,773
I'M JUST GONNA KEEP DOING
WHAT I'M DOING

661
00:25:02,773 --> 00:25:03,774
BECAUSE THE MORE
I THINK ABOUT

662
00:25:03,774 --> 00:25:05,542
WHAT THEY ARE SAYING
TO ME,

663
00:25:05,542 --> 00:25:06,777
THE MORE
IT MAKES ME NERVOUS.

664
00:25:06,777 --> 00:25:08,579
NOW TRY
WITH THE FACE MORE.

665
00:25:08,579 --> 00:25:10,314
JAYLA'S EXPRESSION
IS THIS...

666
00:25:14,184 --> 00:25:15,752
AND FOR A TOP MODEL
TO GIVE ME

667
00:25:15,752 --> 00:25:21,325
THAT SAME FLAT, BORING FACE
TIME AND TIME AGAIN,

668
00:25:21,325 --> 00:25:23,727
I DON'T THINK YOU CAN
HONESTLY STEP OUT

669
00:25:23,727 --> 00:25:26,396
INTO THAT WORLD
WITH ONE EXPRESSION.

670
00:25:26,396 --> 00:25:30,200
JAYLA, I NEED YOUR FACE TO GO
FROM JUST PRETTY

671
00:25:30,200 --> 00:25:31,735
TO HAVING THAT
LITTLE EXTRA SOMETHING

672
00:25:31,735 --> 00:25:34,238
THAT MAKES
PEOPLE GO "WOW."

673
00:25:34,238 --> 00:25:35,606
EVEN THOUGH JAYLA'S
A VERY PRETTY GIRL--

674
00:25:35,606 --> 00:25:37,407
SHE GETS MADE UP,
SHE LOOKS AMAZING--

675
00:25:37,407 --> 00:25:39,843
BUT I DIDN'T FEEL THAT SHE WAS
REALLY HAVING FUN WITH IT.

676
00:25:39,843 --> 00:25:41,445
OWN THIS SHOT.

677
00:25:41,445 --> 00:25:42,846
THERE YOU GO,
JAYLA.

678
00:25:42,846 --> 00:25:44,715
I GOT THE SAME COMMENTS
THAT I GET

679
00:25:44,715 --> 00:25:46,350
EVERY SINGLE ONE
OF MY PHOTO SHOOTS.

680
00:25:46,350 --> 00:25:47,884
SO I'M LIKE, "OH, GREAT,
MY PHOTO SHOOT SUCKS."

681
00:25:49,686 --> 00:25:51,622
I THINK EVERYONE WANTS TO DO
ESPECIALLY WELL TODAY

682
00:25:51,622 --> 00:25:52,956
BECAUSE NIGEL
IS A JUDGE.

683
00:25:52,956 --> 00:25:54,491
ALL RIGHT,
LET'S GO.

684
00:25:54,491 --> 00:25:55,859
SERIOUS FACES
ALL AROUND,

685
00:25:55,859 --> 00:25:59,296
EYES ARE THE ONLY THING
THAT GLITTER.

686
00:25:59,296 --> 00:26:00,464
BEAUTIFUL.

687
00:26:00,464 --> 00:26:01,598
JAY, LET'S
HAVE SOME FAN.

688
00:26:01,598 --> 00:26:02,766
TURN THAT FAN UP HIGH
FOR ME, PLEASE.

689
00:26:02,766 --> 00:26:04,968
ALL IN THE EYES,
PLEASE.

690
00:26:04,968 --> 00:26:06,970
CAN YOU COME
EVEN FURTHER DOWN?

691
00:26:06,970 --> 00:26:08,272
GORGEOUS.

692
00:26:08,272 --> 00:26:09,539
MAKES YOU LOOK
MORE RELAXED.

693
00:26:09,539 --> 00:26:10,841
I DIDN'T THINK THAT NICOLE
WAS REALLY GONNA BE

694
00:26:10,841 --> 00:26:11,908
AS GOOD
AS SHE WAS.

695
00:26:11,908 --> 00:26:13,377
NO FAN, THOUGH.

696
00:26:13,377 --> 00:26:14,811
CAN WE RELEASE
THAT FAN?

697
00:26:14,811 --> 00:26:16,213
FOR ME, SHE REALLY
STEPPED UP HER GAME,

698
00:26:16,213 --> 00:26:18,315
AND WHAT THIS COMPETITION
IS ABOUT

699
00:26:18,315 --> 00:26:21,218
IS ABOUT STEPPING UP YOUR GAME
TIME AND TIME AGAIN.

700
00:26:21,218 --> 00:26:22,853
NOT BECAUSE OF NIGEL
OR ANYTHING,

701
00:26:22,853 --> 00:26:24,454
'CAUSE I'LL
BE DAMNED

702
00:26:24,454 --> 00:26:27,391
IF I GONNA BLOW
HIS HEAD UP BIGGER THAN IT IS.

703
00:26:27,391 --> 00:26:30,327
BUT, NICOLE, THAT WAS, LIKE,
YOUR BEST SHOOT EVER.

704
00:26:31,695 --> 00:26:33,363
TRY AND GIVE ME
SOMETHING PRETTY FACE ON.

705
00:26:33,363 --> 00:26:34,364
OKAY.

706
00:26:34,364 --> 00:26:36,233
ARE WE READY?

707
00:26:36,233 --> 00:26:37,734
GORGEOUS.

708
00:26:37,734 --> 00:26:38,769
REALLY
MOVING WELL.

709
00:26:38,769 --> 00:26:40,437
REALLY MOVING
WELL.

710
00:26:40,437 --> 00:26:41,672
NICE, GUYS.

711
00:26:41,672 --> 00:26:42,873
EVERYBODY'S DOING
A GOOD JOB.

712
00:26:42,873 --> 00:26:43,974
NIK HAD
THE HUNDRED FRAMES.

713
00:26:43,974 --> 00:26:45,375
SHOT NUMBER ONE--
GORGEOUS.

714
00:26:45,375 --> 00:26:46,610
SHOT NUMBER TWO-- GORGEOUS.

715
00:26:46,610 --> 00:26:48,412
SHOT NUMBER THREE--
FLAWLESS.

716
00:26:48,412 --> 00:26:50,514
NIK DIDN'T EVEN NEED
THOSE EXTRA FRAMES TODAY.

717
00:26:50,514 --> 00:26:53,884
OKAY, GUYS,
LAST FRAME.

718
00:26:53,884 --> 00:26:56,453
WHOO--
ALL RIGHT!

719
00:26:58,722 --> 00:27:00,357
WE FINISH
THE PHOTO SHOOT,

720
00:27:00,357 --> 00:27:03,260
AND WE'RE TOLD THAT WE ARE GOING
OUT TO DINNER TONIGHT.

721
00:27:03,260 --> 00:27:06,563
IT'S DEFINITELY MY FIRST TIME
IN AN INDIAN RESTAURANT.

722
00:27:06,563 --> 00:27:08,799
BUT I'M JUST LOOKING FORWARD
TO, YOU KNOW, NEW THINGS.

723
00:27:12,969 --> 00:27:14,438
WOULD YOU LIKE TO
HEAR OUR SPECIALS?

724
00:27:14,438 --> 00:27:16,373
HEY, LADIES.

725
00:27:16,373 --> 00:27:17,574
HI, NIGEL.

726
00:27:17,574 --> 00:27:18,375
HOW
ARE YA?

727
00:27:18,375 --> 00:27:18,875
GOOD.

728
00:27:18,875 --> 00:27:20,711
I'M GOING TO BE ONE OF
YOUR OTHER GUESTS TONIGHT.

729
00:27:20,711 --> 00:27:21,511
IT'S A FUN
SURPRISE.

730
00:27:21,511 --> 00:27:23,347
IT'S REALLY COOL THAT WE GET
TO SEE NIGEL AWAY FROM PANEL.

731
00:27:23,347 --> 00:27:26,750
AND HE IS ACTUALLY
HUMAN TO US NOW.

732
00:27:26,750 --> 00:27:28,952
MY MOTHER IS
FROM SRI LANKA,

733
00:27:28,952 --> 00:27:30,587
AND SHE WAS ALSO
A MODEL

734
00:27:30,587 --> 00:27:32,622
AND SHE BROUGHT HER FAMILY OVER
FROM SRI LANKA

735
00:27:32,622 --> 00:27:35,592
TO ENGLAND BECAUSE OF THE MONEY
SHE MADE FROM MODELING.

736
00:27:35,592 --> 00:27:37,394
AND I'D LIKE TO INTRODUCE YOU
TO MY MOTHER.

737
00:27:37,394 --> 00:27:38,895
SHE'S GONNA
HAVE DINNER WITH US.

738
00:27:38,895 --> 00:27:41,398
MUM--
THIS IS MY MOTHER.

739
00:27:41,398 --> 00:27:42,799
NICE TO MEET YOU.

740
00:27:42,799 --> 00:27:44,501
THIS IS A LOVELY TREAT
FOR ME.

741
00:27:44,501 --> 00:27:46,603
I GET TO SPEND TIME
WITH NIGEL.

742
00:27:46,603 --> 00:27:47,904
EXACTLY.

743
00:27:47,904 --> 00:27:50,307
I WAS BORN IN BOMBAY,
WHICH IS NOW CALLED MUMBAI.

744
00:27:50,307 --> 00:27:52,509
I STARTED
MY SINGING CAREER AT 14.

745
00:27:52,509 --> 00:27:54,878
AND THEN I WON
A MODELING COMPETITION AS WELL.

746
00:27:54,878 --> 00:27:57,714
YOU'VE GOT TO FOLLOW YOUR HEART
AND LEARN AS MUCH AS YOU CAN,

747
00:27:57,714 --> 00:28:00,250
BECAUSE THAT WILL STAND YOU
IN GOOD STEAD.

748
00:28:00,250 --> 00:28:02,519
I ENJOYED HAVING
DINNER WITH NIGEL AND HIS MOM.

749
00:28:02,519 --> 00:28:04,521
SHE KIND OF MAKES ME
FEEL A LOT BETTER.

750
00:28:04,521 --> 00:28:06,556
YOU GUYS ALL SAW SARIS TODAY,
DIDN'T YOU?

751
00:28:06,556 --> 00:28:07,858
PERHAPS YOU'D LIKE TO SHOW THEM
HOW TO PUT ON THE SARI.

752
00:28:07,858 --> 00:28:09,593
YES.

753
00:28:09,593 --> 00:28:13,196
NOW A SARI IS MADE UP
OF 6 YARDS OF MATERIAL,

754
00:28:13,196 --> 00:28:16,600
AND IT'S VERY EASY TO DRAPE
ONCE YOU GET THE HANG OF IT.

755
00:28:16,600 --> 00:28:19,803
NIGEL'S MOTHER IS TEACHING US
HOW TO WEAR SARIS.

756
00:28:19,803 --> 00:28:22,272
I'M DEFINITELY PAYING ATTENTION
BECAUSE FOR SOME REASON,

757
00:28:22,272 --> 00:28:25,542
I FEEL LIKE SOMEHOW THIS IS
GONNA COME BACK LATER ON.

758
00:28:25,542 --> 00:28:27,411
SEE HOW ELEGANT
YOU LOOK?

759
00:28:27,411 --> 00:28:28,512
SO THERE YOU GO,
GUYS.

760
00:28:28,512 --> 00:28:30,614
THAT'S THE SECRETS
TO THE SARI.

761
00:28:30,614 --> 00:28:31,615
GOOD NIGHT.

762
00:28:31,615 --> 00:28:32,616
GOOD NIGHT.

763
00:28:32,616 --> 00:28:34,418
GOOD NIGHT.

764
00:28:37,454 --> 00:28:39,423
TYRA MAIL.

765
00:28:39,423 --> 00:28:41,391
"TOMORROW YOU
WILL MEET WITH THE JUDGES.

766
00:28:41,391 --> 00:28:43,627
"ONLY THREE OF YOU
WILL CONTINUE ON

767
00:28:43,627 --> 00:28:46,696
"IN THE HOPE OF BECOMING
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

768
00:28:46,696 --> 00:28:49,232
"ONE OF YOU WILL BE
ELIMINATED.

769
00:28:49,232 --> 00:28:50,333
"TYRA."

770
00:28:50,333 --> 00:28:52,836
"X-O. X-O, TYRA."

771
00:28:52,836 --> 00:28:54,838
COME ON, NOW,
READ IT RIGHT.

772
00:28:54,838 --> 00:28:56,540
YOU KNOW WHAT?

773
00:28:56,540 --> 00:28:58,708
I WOULD KNOW WHETHER
I WAS DOING GOOD OR DOING BAD

774
00:28:58,708 --> 00:29:00,811
IF I UNDERSTOOD WHAT WAS GOING
THROUGH THE JUDGES' HEADS.

775
00:29:00,811 --> 00:29:02,546
I HONESTLY NEVER REALLY FEEL
THAT COMFORTABLE

776
00:29:02,546 --> 00:29:03,847
WHERE I AM
IN THE COMPETITION.

777
00:29:03,847 --> 00:29:05,515
I DON'T KNOW.

778
00:29:05,515 --> 00:29:07,717
IT WOULD REALLY SUCK
TO BE SENT HOME RIGHT NOW.

779
00:29:07,717 --> 00:29:09,753
WHY AM I
STILL HERE?

780
00:29:09,753 --> 00:29:11,655
I MADE IT
TO THE TOP FOUR.

781
00:29:11,655 --> 00:29:15,859
I MAY NOT BE HERE TOMORROW, BUT
WHETHER WE REALIZE THIS OR NOT.

782
00:29:15,859 --> 00:29:18,195
I'M THE FOURTH BADDEST BITCH
IN AMERICA,

783
00:29:18,195 --> 00:29:20,263
AND AIN'T NOBODY
TAKING THAT AWAY FROM ME.

784
00:29:25,602 --> 00:29:28,672
♪♪♪

785
00:29:28,672 --> 00:29:30,574
I HAVE BEEN DRAGGED
THROUGH THE DIRT

786
00:29:30,574 --> 00:29:32,642
EVERY SINGLE
ELIMINATION.

787
00:29:32,642 --> 00:29:34,611
FIRST TIME I WAS IN
THE BOTTOM TWO,

788
00:29:34,611 --> 00:29:35,946
I WAS SHOCKED.

789
00:29:35,946 --> 00:29:37,948
WILL DIANE AND BRE
PLEASE STEP FORWARD?

790
00:29:37,948 --> 00:29:39,783
SECOND TIME I WAS
IN THE BOTTOM TWO,

791
00:29:39,783 --> 00:29:41,284
I FELT
DEFEATED.

792
00:29:41,284 --> 00:29:42,819
WILL BRE AND KYLE
PLEASE STEP FORWARD?

793
00:29:42,819 --> 00:29:44,287
THIRD TIME I WAS IN
THE BOTTOM TWO,

794
00:29:44,354 --> 00:29:45,722
I COMPLETELY
WENT NUMB,

795
00:29:45,722 --> 00:29:47,657
AND I JUST WANTED
TO DIE.

796
00:29:47,657 --> 00:29:49,693
WILL BRE AND KIM
PLEASE STEP FORWARD?

797
00:29:49,693 --> 00:29:52,963
I AM THE UNDERDOG OF
"AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL."

798
00:29:52,963 --> 00:29:55,365
I DON'T KNOW IF I'M GONNA WIN
THIS COMPETITION,

799
00:29:55,365 --> 00:29:57,968
BUT DO I DESERVE
TO WIN THE COMPETITION?

800
00:29:57,968 --> 00:29:59,302
YES.

801
00:30:12,716 --> 00:30:14,284
WELCOME,
LADIES.

802
00:30:14,284 --> 00:30:15,418
YOU GUYS
LOOK LOVELY.

803
00:30:15,418 --> 00:30:17,587
NOW IT'S TIME TO MAKE OUR
NINTH CUT,

804
00:30:17,587 --> 00:30:19,556
WHICH WILL
BRING US ONE STEP CLOSER

805
00:30:19,556 --> 00:30:21,424
TOWARDS DETERMINING
WHO WILL BECOME

806
00:30:21,424 --> 00:30:23,894
AMERICA'S NEXT
TOP MODEL.

807
00:30:23,894 --> 00:30:27,397
AND, OF COURSE,
WE HAVE LOVELY DOVELY PRIZES.

808
00:30:27,397 --> 00:30:29,266
THE FIRST IS
A MODELING CONTRACT

809
00:30:29,266 --> 00:30:32,202
WITH TOP MANAGEMENT COMPANY
FORD MODELS,

810
00:30:32,202 --> 00:30:33,770
A SPREAD IN
"ELLE" MAGAZINE,

811
00:30:33,770 --> 00:30:35,305
WHICH WILL BE
SHOT BY

812
00:30:35,305 --> 00:30:37,340
WORLD-RENOWNED
PHOTOGRAPHER GILLES BENSIMON

813
00:30:37,340 --> 00:30:41,344
AND A COVER OF
"ELLEgirl" MAGAZINE,

814
00:30:41,344 --> 00:30:45,248
WHICH HITS STANDS
IN FEBRUARY, 2006.

815
00:30:45,248 --> 00:30:46,650
AND LAST,
BUT NOT LEAST,

816
00:30:46,650 --> 00:30:51,788
A CONTRACT WORTH $100,000
FROM COVER GIRL COSMETICS.

817
00:30:51,788 --> 00:30:53,423
AND, OF COURSE, YOU KNOW
OUR JUDGES...

818
00:30:53,423 --> 00:30:54,658
MR. NIGEL BARKER...

819
00:30:54,658 --> 00:30:56,326
HI, LADIES.

820
00:30:56,326 --> 00:30:57,761
NOTED FASHION PHOTOGRAPHER
THAT SHOT YOU THIS WEEK.

821
00:30:57,761 --> 00:31:00,630
LEGENDARY, LOVELY

822
00:31:00,630 --> 00:31:01,731
MISS
J. ALEXANDER,

823
00:31:01,731 --> 00:31:04,200
YOUR RUNWAY COACH.

824
00:31:04,200 --> 00:31:06,503
MISS TWIGGY,
FASHION ICON.

825
00:31:06,503 --> 00:31:09,239
AND BARBARA HULANICKI.

826
00:31:09,239 --> 00:31:11,875
BARBARA IS THE CREATOR
AND DESIGNER OF BIBA,

827
00:31:11,875 --> 00:31:16,780
AND BARBARA PUT MOD ON THE MAP
SINGLE-HANDEDLY.

828
00:31:16,780 --> 00:31:18,248
NOW THIS WEEK

829
00:31:18,248 --> 00:31:19,816
YOU GUYS LEARNED ABOUT
FOUR INFLUENTIAL FASHIONS,

830
00:31:19,816 --> 00:31:21,351
DID YOU NOT?

831
00:31:21,351 --> 00:31:22,752
YOU'RE GONNA BE PUT
TO THE TEST.

832
00:31:22,752 --> 00:31:25,422
THERE IS AN ITEM THAT HAS
INSPIRED LONDON DESIGNERS

833
00:31:25,422 --> 00:31:28,425
THAT WAITS IN THE BACK FOR YOU
RIGHT NOW.

834
00:31:28,425 --> 00:31:30,460
YOU HAVE THREE MINUTES
TO TAKE THAT ITEM

835
00:31:30,460 --> 00:31:33,797
AND UPDATE IT
TO MODERN FASHION.

836
00:31:33,797 --> 00:31:34,965
ARE YOU READY?

837
00:31:34,965 --> 00:31:35,899
GO!

838
00:31:36,967 --> 00:31:39,436
♪♪♪

839
00:31:54,284 --> 00:31:57,487
ALL RIGHTY.
FIRST IS NICOLE.

840
00:31:57,487 --> 00:32:00,657
SO, NICOLE, YOU HAD TO DO
SOMETHING WITH THE SARI

841
00:32:00,657 --> 00:32:01,691
THAT'S MODERN.

842
00:32:01,691 --> 00:32:02,626
GIVE A LITTLE TWIRL,
DARLING.

843
00:32:02,626 --> 00:32:04,194
LITTLE TWIRL.

844
00:32:04,194 --> 00:32:05,528
I LIKE THAT
THE BOOTY'S OUT.

845
00:32:05,528 --> 00:32:07,464
IT LOOKS LIKE YOU FELL IN
THE CURTAINS OR SOMETHING.

846
00:32:07,464 --> 00:32:08,565
ALL WRAPPED UP
LIKE A CAT,

847
00:32:08,565 --> 00:32:10,300
LIKE RAWR!

848
00:32:10,300 --> 00:32:11,635
YOU'RE COVERING TOO MUCH
OF YOURSELF.

849
00:32:11,635 --> 00:32:12,902
I'M WITH NIGEL.

850
00:32:12,902 --> 00:32:14,638
I WOULD JUST TAKE
EVERYTHING OFF

851
00:32:14,638 --> 00:32:16,272
AND JUST
TIE IT UP.

852
00:32:16,272 --> 00:32:17,540
SO WHEN
YOU TURNED ROUND,

853
00:32:17,540 --> 00:32:19,743
WE GOT BARE BACK
AND A LITTLE BUTT CLEAVAGE.

854
00:32:19,743 --> 00:32:21,778
THEN IT WOULD
BE GOOD.

855
00:32:21,778 --> 00:32:22,879
WHY ARE YOU
SO HORNY?

856
00:32:22,879 --> 00:32:24,414
WELL,
YOU KNOW...

857
00:32:24,414 --> 00:32:26,950
ALL RIGHTY, NICOLE,
HERE IS YOUR BEST SHOT.

858
00:32:26,950 --> 00:32:29,419
WELL, FOR ME,
YOU PHOTOGRAPHED

859
00:32:29,419 --> 00:32:31,354
ALL THE WAY THROUGH
THE COMPETITION BRILLIANTLY.

860
00:32:31,354 --> 00:32:33,723
I MEAN, YOU ARE VERY,
VERY PHOTOGENIC.

861
00:32:33,723 --> 00:32:36,459
I DON'T SEE NOTHING REALLY
INTENSE ABOUT THAT PICTURE.

862
00:32:36,459 --> 00:32:37,494
I JUST--

863
00:32:37,494 --> 00:32:38,862
REALLY?

864
00:32:38,862 --> 00:32:40,363
SHE COULD BE
MUCH MORE BEAUTIFUL, PERSONALLY,

865
00:32:40,363 --> 00:32:42,332
FOR ME,
UP CLOSE.

866
00:32:42,332 --> 00:32:45,435
I HAVE TO 100% DISAGREE
WITH MISS J.

867
00:32:45,435 --> 00:32:47,871
YOU HAVE NEVER HAD
THIS MUCH RANGE.

868
00:32:47,871 --> 00:32:49,572
I MEAN,
I DIDN'T KNOW WHAT TO CHOOSE.

869
00:32:49,572 --> 00:32:50,974
YOU HAD ONE WHERE
YOU WERE LIKE THIS

870
00:32:50,974 --> 00:32:52,275
AND THEN LIKE THIS,
AND THEN LIKE THIS

871
00:32:52,275 --> 00:32:54,678
AND THEN LIKE THIS,
AND THEN--

872
00:32:54,678 --> 00:32:56,579
I WAS LIKE,
GIRL, YOU BETTER WORK.

873
00:32:56,579 --> 00:32:57,947
THIS IS
YOUR BEST.

874
00:32:57,947 --> 00:32:59,382
MAMA IS PROUD
OF YOU.

875
00:32:59,382 --> 00:33:00,417
MM-HMM.

876
00:33:00,417 --> 00:33:01,418
I LOVE IT.

877
00:33:01,418 --> 00:33:03,720
ALL RIGHT,
UP NEXT IS BRE.

878
00:33:03,720 --> 00:33:05,422
WELL, I DON'T
REALLY KNOW.

879
00:33:05,422 --> 00:33:07,624
BUT IT LOOKS THE MOST
TRADITIONALLY SARI-ISH.

880
00:33:07,624 --> 00:33:09,292
IT'S NOT
A MODERN TAKE.

881
00:33:09,292 --> 00:33:10,794
IT IS ACTUALLY
VERY STRAIGHTFORWARD,

882
00:33:10,794 --> 00:33:12,462
AND HEY,
THAT'S YOU.

883
00:33:12,462 --> 00:33:13,563
AND NO SHOES.

884
00:33:13,563 --> 00:33:14,564
NO SHOES.

885
00:33:14,564 --> 00:33:15,765
ALL RIGHT,
BRE.

886
00:33:15,765 --> 00:33:17,434
SO YOU GUYS
HAD A PHOTO SHOOT THIS WEEK

887
00:33:17,434 --> 00:33:20,937
WHERE YOU HAD TO BE A FACE
IN A CROWD.

888
00:33:20,937 --> 00:33:23,940
HERE'S
YOUR BEST SHOT.

889
00:33:23,940 --> 00:33:26,476
WELL, ACTUALLY
YOU DO JUMP OUT.

890
00:33:26,476 --> 00:33:28,845
MY EYES WENT STRAIGHT
TO YOU.

891
00:33:28,845 --> 00:33:31,815
IF THAT WAS THE CHALLENGE,
YOU GOT IT, GIRL.

892
00:33:31,815 --> 00:33:34,184
OOH, I SOUNDED
ALL AMERICAN THEN.

893
00:33:34,184 --> 00:33:35,819
BRE, BECAUSE YOU ARE
A LITTLE BIT SHORTER

894
00:33:35,819 --> 00:33:37,220
THAN
THE AVERAGE MODEL,

895
00:33:37,220 --> 00:33:39,622
YOU HAVE TO
REMEMBER YOUR NECK

896
00:33:39,622 --> 00:33:41,891
BECAUSE THAT'S THE ONE THING
THAT MAKES THIS PHOTO NOT A TEN,

897
00:33:41,891 --> 00:33:43,626
IS THAT YOUR NECK
LOOKS SHORT.

898
00:33:43,626 --> 00:33:45,795
JAY SAID THAT YOU WEREN'T
THE SAME BRE

899
00:33:45,795 --> 00:33:47,330
THAT HE'S USED
TO SEEING

900
00:33:47,330 --> 00:33:48,965
AND DON'T TAKE A BENADRYL
BEFORE A PHOTO SHOOT.

901
00:33:48,965 --> 00:33:50,333
IT'LL MAKE YOU
TIRED.

902
00:33:50,333 --> 00:33:51,568
YOU TOOK
A BENADRYL?

903
00:33:51,568 --> 00:33:52,736
I THOUGHT IT WAS, LIKE,
AN ALLERGY--

904
00:33:52,736 --> 00:33:54,504
LIKE A SINUS
INFECTION,

905
00:33:54,504 --> 00:33:57,340
AND SO ONE OF THE GIRLS
GAVE ME A BENADRYL.

906
00:33:57,340 --> 00:33:59,809
YOU LET A GIRL
GIVE YOU A PILL?

907
00:33:59,809 --> 00:34:01,211
YOUR COMPETITION?

908
00:34:01,211 --> 00:34:02,345
NO, IT WAS--

909
00:34:02,345 --> 00:34:03,713
(laughter)

910
00:34:03,713 --> 00:34:04,948
YOU LET YOUR COMPETITION
GIVE YOU A PILL, GIRL?

911
00:34:04,948 --> 00:34:06,449
BUT I DON'T HAVE
ANY MEDICINE

912
00:34:06,449 --> 00:34:07,584
TO TAKE
WHILE I'M OUT HERE,

913
00:34:07,584 --> 00:34:08,618
AND I KEEP GETTING SICK,
SO...

914
00:34:08,618 --> 00:34:09,652
MM-HMM.

915
00:34:09,652 --> 00:34:11,287
UP NEXT IS NIK.

916
00:34:12,856 --> 00:34:17,526
TO ME, THAT'S THE KIND
OF MOST MODERN, UNIQUE WAY OF--

917
00:34:17,526 --> 00:34:19,361
I WOULDN'T HAVE KNOWN
IT WAS A SARI, ACTUALLY.

918
00:34:19,361 --> 00:34:20,629
BUT I GOTTA TELL YOU
ONE THING,

919
00:34:20,629 --> 00:34:22,665
YOU PICKED A COLOR THAT'S
GOOD FOR YOUR SKIN.

